From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Filippo Falezza <filippo.falezza@outlook.it>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 00:52:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 111/113] LOCAL: drm/sysfb: simpledrm: Attach power domains
 before enabling clocks

Clocks inside a collapsed power domain can't turn on: with the MDSS
GDSC listed, enabling the display clocks first fails with "status stuck
at 'off'".

These changes were written with the help of an LLM and checked by a human.

Assisted-by: LLM dtschema
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RmfiVDW3KWZdb9c3iDGRYg
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/sysfb/simpledrm.c | 7 ++++---
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/sysfb/simpledrm.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/sysfb/simpledrm.c
index dc992e1dc..c9cef2334 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/sysfb/simpledrm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/sysfb/simpledrm.c
@@ -724,13 +724,14 @@ static struct simpledrm_device *simpledrm_device_create(struct drm_driver *drv,
 	 * Hardware settings
 	 */
 
-	ret = simpledrm_device_init_clocks(sdev);
+	/* Power domains first: clocks inside a collapsed domain can't turn on */
+	ret = simpledrm_device_attach_genpd(sdev);
 	if (ret)
 		return ERR_PTR(ret);
-	ret = simpledrm_device_init_regulators(sdev);
+	ret = simpledrm_device_init_clocks(sdev);
 	if (ret)
 		return ERR_PTR(ret);
-	ret = simpledrm_device_attach_genpd(sdev);
+	ret = simpledrm_device_init_regulators(sdev);
 	if (ret)
 		return ERR_PTR(ret);
 	if (of_node) {
